Subject: [PATCH] Keep SYSTEMROOT and SYSTEMDRIVE in the strict repo env on
 Windows (#32440)

Keep SYSTEMROOT and SYSTEMDRIVE in the strict repo env on Windows

### Description

On Windows, `--experimental_strict_repo_env` now keeps `SYSTEMDRIVE` and
`SYSTEMROOT` in the repository environment, next to `PATH` and `PATHEXT`.

#27745 removed the shell test of the strict environment. I can restore
it with checks for the two variables if you want one here.

### Motivation

A process that `ctx.execute` starts under the strict mode runs without
`SYSTEMROOT`. Winsock expands `%SystemRoot%` in the paths of its
providers, so every DNS lookup in that process fails. `go mod download`
in Gazelle's `go_repository` fails with `getaddrinfow: A non-recoverable
error occurred during a database lookup`.

`WindowsSubprocessFactory` adds both variables to every process, but it
reads them from the environment that the caller passes. For
`ctx.execute`, that is the already filtered repository environment, so
the fallback finds nothing.

The two variables describe the operating system, not the user, like
`PATHEXT`. They stay visible in `ctx.os.environ`, and
`--repo_env==SYSTEMROOT` removes them. Making the fallback in
`WindowsSubprocessFactory` independent of the caller would change every
Windows subprocess of Bazel, so it is left for a separate change.

Fixes #32439

### Build API Changes

No

